{
    "background_story": "Caden was a contractor with a reputation for cutting corners. He would often bid low on projects, only to use subpar materials and rush through the work. His shoddiness was notorious among homeowners, who would later discover leaks, cracks, and other defects in the work he had done. Despite the complaints, Caden continued to operate with a 'good enough' attitude, prioritizing profits over quality. However, his luck ran out when he was hired to renovate a historic mansion. The owner, a meticulous preservationist, was appalled by Caden's sloppy work and sued him for damages. The court ruling not only cost Caden his business but also his reputation. His name became synonymous with shoddiness, a cautionary tale of the importance of integrity and craftsmanship.",
